  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/... \nExtreme Heat is expected to impact much of the area late this \nweek through at least the weekend as the subtropical ridge \nstrengthens while the center gradually shifts over the region \nFriday into Saturday. Record or near record climatological H5 \nheights are forecast across New Mexico starting Thursday, \neventually moving into Arizona Friday into Saturday with H5 \nheights potentially reaching 598-600dm over Arizona. Major \nHeatRisk is expected to impact all of the lower deserts starting \nThursday, becoming even more widespread Friday into the weekend as\nlocalized areas of Extreme HeatRisk may develop. The forecast \nhighs of 110-116 degrees Thursday through next Monday (below \nrecords) is masking the potential severity of this heat wave as \ndew points and humidities are expected to remain elevated. Heat \nindices are likely to reach 113-120 degrees over the lower deserts\nstarting Friday with the highest readings across southwest \nArizona and southeast California. Overnight lows will also become \nvery warm with readings not likely falling much below the upper \n80s. Lower 90s can be expected for much of the urban core of \nPhoenix starting Thursday night. If we do end up mixing out more \nof the boundary layer moisture, the higher end of NBM guidance \nshows highs potentially reaching 116-118 degrees in the Phoenix \narea to as high as 117-120 degrees for portions of southeast \nCalifornia.\n\nThe hottest days are likely to be Friday-Sunday, but there is more\nforecast uncertainty by Sunday as some guidance indicates some\nmoisture return this weekend and the potential for more \nconvective activity. For now, we are not expecting much if any \nhigh terrain showers or thunderstorms Thursday and Friday, but \nthat could change starting Saturday or Sunday. Any more extensive \nconvective activity may eventually disrupt the extreme heat, at \nleast over eastern and possibly into central Arizona by Sunday or \nMonday. If we don't get relief from storm activity, guidance at \nleast heavily favors some weakening of the ridge early next week \nwhile also shifting it farther to the east.",
